text:
Maya: Heads-up: I'm iterating on the mobile console layout—need quick UX review on breakpoints, table overflow, and sidebar behavior. Screenshot: https://img.redwood.ai/s/console-mobile-v3.png  Thoughts? cc @Kevin @Liz

Kevin: Looks promising! main question: prefer collapsing left nav to bottom tabs or a hamburger + slide-over? :thinking:

Maya: Leaning bottom tabs because primary routes are 4-5. Slide-over hides too much of the workspace. Also worried about touch targets on current 32px buttons — should be larger. :point_up:

Liz: +1 to bottom tabs. Accessibility wise we need clear aria-labels and focus order. For tables: I think horizontal scroll with sticky header + pinned 'primary' column works better than stacking rows.

Kevin: For narrow widths can we set column priority and hide low-priority cols? Example:
```css
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .table { overflow-x: auto; }
  .col[data-priority="low"] { display: none; }
}
```
This keeps the important columns visible and avoids weird wrapping.

ProductopsBot: Deploy preview available: https://staging.redwood.ai/console/mobile-v3 — build #2318

Maya: Nice. Can someone smoke-test keyboard navigation and VoiceOver? I'm worried about tab order when bottom nav is present (tabbing through content then hitting bottom nav shouldn't trap focus).

Sam: I'll run a quick a11y pass. On iOS VoiceOver the bottom nav needs semantic order and use of aria-current on the active tab. Also make sure roles: role="tablist" / role="tab" for proper announcements.

Liz: UX nit: reduce table row density on mobile — increase vertical padding to 12-16px for comfortable tap targets. Also ensure the pinned column has visual separation (subtle divider) so scrolled content reads correctly.

Kevin: One more: prefer breakpoint at 720px rather than 640px — a lot of midrange Android phones report ~720dp width. Can we make breakpoint configurable via a variable?

Maya: Good call. I'll switch to a variable: $mobile-breakpoint: 720px and test both. Quick CSS piece I plan to add:
```css
$mobile-breakpoint: 720px;
@media (max-width: #{$mobile-breakpoint}) {
  /* bottom nav styles, table adjustments */
}
```
I'll open a PR in a few mins.

Design-bot: PR linked: https://github.com/redwood-inference/console/pull/482 — reviewers @Liz @Kevin

Liz: I'll review this afternoon. If accessible and layout tests pass, merge and schedule a canary rollout. :+1:

Kevin: If merged, let's add a telemetry event "mobile_layout" with variant (bottom-tabs / slide-over) so we can measure engagement/retention differences.

Maya: Sounds good — I'll add the telemetry spike and a short test plan in the PR description. Thanks everyone for the quick feedback!
